# Voice casting for the friends. A rule names characters (id or display name), names character
# tags, or is the default. Resolution: character > tags (most matches) > default.
#
# friend-a is voiced but not yet *spoken*: the friends have no audio path until GROUP.md slice 6.
# This rule exists now so the voice is pinned data -- docs/PERSONA.md and tests/test_persona.py
# both compare against it, and a mismatch is a failing test rather than a surprise on game night.
#
# TUNED 2026-10-22, twice. First attempt: ryan at 1.15, reported "too fast, not deep enough".
# Second: ryan at 1.2 with pitch 0.93 -- the resample coloured the voice and read as off.
# Now: a naturally deep voice instead of a shifted one. Measured median F0 over the same
# sentence: ryan-high 144 Hz, joe-medium 98 Hz, norman-medium 95 Hz (see docs/PERSONA.md 3d).
# `pitch` is deliberately 1.0 -- no resampling, so the timbre is the model's own.
#
# The brief: deep, American, clear and cheerful -- a bass Santa Claus. Piper's length_scale runs
# the other way round: 1.0 is normal and higher is slower, so a little above 1 is unhurried.
# 1.05, not 1.2: joe already reads slower than ryan did at neutral (6.9 s vs 6.0 s for the test
# sentence), and 1.2 on top of that was reported "a hair too slow".
#
# VERIFIED 2026-10-22: the model is downloaded (in the tts model cache, not the repo), 22 kHz mono,
# a twenty-word line renders in about 5.5 s at roughly 0.4x realtime on this CPU.
{"id": "cast-topguy", "characters": ["friend-a", "TopGuy"], "engine": "piper", "voice": "en_US-joe-medium", "speed": 1.05, "volume": 1.0}
